  "term": "ethyl alcohol",
  "definition": "Ethyl alcohol is a fermented, volatile chemical substance that slows central nervous system activity. It also promotes fluid loss by reducing antidiuretic hormone and can act as a disinfectant by breaking down proteins in microorganisms.",
